{
  "project": {
    "name": "Hook-and-Loop Tape",
    "slug": "hook-loop-tape",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "engine": "cadquery",
    "description": {
      "en": "A printable analogue of hook-and-loop tape: two mating strips that peel apart and re-close. The hook strip carries a field of mushroom-headed pins; the loop strip carries a waffle grid of thin walls whose cells those heads snag on. This is the rigid hard good the Fashion Cabinet `hook-loop-tape` hardware reference bridges to — a garment's finished closure overlap drives the strip, and the garment keeps the placement math.\n\nOfficial Visualizer and Configurator: Yantra4D",
      "es": "Un análogo imprimible de la cinta de gancho y bucle (velcro): dos tiras que se despegan y vuelven a cerrar. La tira de ganchos lleva un campo de pines con cabeza de hongo; la tira de bucles lleva una retícula de paredes delgadas en cuyas celdas se enganchan esas cabezas. Este es el herraje rígido al que se puentea el avío `hook-loop-tape` de Fashion Cabinet — el traslape terminado de la prenda determina la tira, y la prenda conserva el cálculo de colocación.\n\nVisualizador y configurador oficial: Yantra4D"
    },
    "thumbnail": "/projects/hook-loop-tape.webp",
    "difficulty": "intermediate",
